course: dictionary
lesson: 11800
title: Beset
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When trouble keeps coming at you from every side, writers say you are beset. «The journey was beset by problems» means there were many problems on the way, all troubling the travellers. Beset is a verb, so it changes form: beset, besets, beset, besetting.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Beset is nearly always used with «by» or «with», as in «beset by» or «beset with». «The castle was beset with dangers» tells you the dangers were all around. The words after «by» or «with» tell you what is causing the trouble.
explain: In older stories, beset has a stronger meaning: to surround and attack. «The travellers were beset by robbers in the dark forest» means the robbers came at them from all sides. To check your meaning, swap in «troubled on all sides». If it fits the sentence, you have understood it.
fact: Beset means to have many troubles, dangers or worries troubling you from all sides.
fact: «The journey was beset by problems» means the trip had many problems.
fact: In old tales, «beset» can mean to surround and attack someone.
fact: Beset is usually used with «by» or «with»: «beset by fears», «beset with dangers».
fact: Mole in The Wind in the Willows is beset by fears in the Wild Wood.
exercise: «The climb was beset by strong winds and slippery rocks.» What does beset mean here? | *Troubled on every side by problems | Cheered on by a crowd | Made smooth and easy | Tidied up neatly
exercise: «The farmer was beset by worries about the dry weather.» Which word shows the farmer had many worries? | weather | dry | *beset | farmer
exercise: «The old knight was beset by robbers on the road.» In this old-tale sense, what does beset mean? | To sing loudly | To give a present | *To surround and attack | To fall fast asleep
test: «The hikers were beset by rain, mud and tiredness.» What does beset mean here? | Lit up by bright lamps | *Troubled on all sides by problems | Given a warm welcome | Carried home on a cart
test: Which words usually come after beset? | *by or with | in or out | after or before | up or down
exam: «Mole was beset by fears in the Wild Wood.» Which word is closest in meaning to beset here? | Cleaned | Blessed | *Troubled | Freed
